                {
                    "path": "https://mediatum.ub.tum.de/doc/1355829/file.pdf",
                    "title": "Aging of Lithium-Ion Batteries in Electric Vehicles",
                    "authors": [],
                    "description": "Based on the findings of the different aging studies, recommendations for optimized operational strategies are derived which enable a long battery life. This thesis demonstrates that at moderate operating temperatures, the required battery life can already be achieved with the state-of-the-art battery types. However, operating at low temperatures of 10degree celsius and below remains challenging. Iproved types of lithium-ion cells and constructive means of thermal conditioning have to be eveloped to overcome the cycle life limitations at low temperatures.",
